caption: Required Reusable Drive Sets
rule: required-reusable-drive-sets

Every completed Domain, World, Pantheon, and Culture defines exactly five canonical Drives.

The list is ordered. Drive 1 is the source's most central behavioral expression, followed by the next most central Drives in descending order.

A campaign using N Drives per source takes Drives 1 through N. Players do not choose later Drives in place of earlier Drives unless the campaign explicitly creates a different rule.

A source contributes Drives when:

The campaign enables that source category.

The source is eligible under the campaign's rules.

The player selects it as an active source, where selection is required.

Finished GATES source documents should include their five Drives directly or link to one authoritative Drive-set entry. Empty or unfinished Drive fields provide no Drives.

A GM who wants more than five Drives from a source may create additional campaign-specific Drives. Reusable source designers are not required to provide more than five.
